# GitHub issue #11

**Repository:** alexisNorthcoders/snake-colyseus
**URL:** https://github.com/alexisNorthcoders/snake-colyseus/issues/11
**State:** OPEN
**Labels:** ready-for-agent
**Title:** Support 4-player rounds

## Body
## What to build

A room should accept four players and play a correct four-player round end to end.

The cap is currently two. Raising it is a one-line change, but it is only safe once the spawn table and head-to-head collision are fixed — the spawn table holds exactly four entries with one cell duplicated, and the index wraps modulo four, so a four-player round would put two snakes on the same cell *every* round. With no head-to-head detection those two then travel in permanent lockstep for the whole round.

The client needs no changes: the scoreboard already iterates all players, starting is a button rather than a two-player gate, and rankings render whatever the server sends.

## Acceptance criteria

- [ ] A room accepts four players; a fifth is routed to a new room
- [ ] All four spawn on distinct cells, every round, across repeated rounds
- [ ] The live scoreboard shows all four players and their scores
- [ ] Game over fires when one player is left, with correct winner and full four-player rankings
- [ ] Repeated rounds ("play again") work with four players, including after someone leaves mid-round

## Blocked by

- #6 Give every snake a distinct spawn cell
- #10 Detect head-to-head collisions
